CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^.*invalid implicit conversion from .* to 'struct pair'.*$
^.*invalid implicit conversion from .* to 'struct initializer_list'.*$
^.*invalid implicit conversion from .* to 'struct _Node_handle.*$
^.*does not uniquely resolve.*$
--
Verifies brace-init-list overload resolution for `std::pair`-typed
parameters: by-value, by-const-lvalue-reference, and by-rvalue-
reference.  All three list-initialise a `std::pair<K, V>` from
`{k, idx}`.  The relevant standard rules are
[over.match.list]/2.2, [over.ics.list]/4, and [over.ics.rank]/
3.3.4.  Without the fix, CBMC's overload resolution would either
prefer an `insert(initializer_list<value_type>)` overload (whose
viability check skipped the per-element ICS to value_type) or
report ambiguity between `(const value_type&)` and `(value_type&&)`
for prvalue source.
